      "title": [
        "mask",
        "mask",
        "mask"
      ],
      "dcDescription": [
        "1916.9.306\n\nName and identification of character\nThe mask depicts the demon of blood, riri yaka (Sin.).\n\nContext\nThis demon mask is used in a demon ceremony known by several names: Riddi yagaya, Rata yakuma, and Kalas vaidde (Sin.).\n\nMaterial\nWood, vel-kaduru (Sin.) (Nux vomica).\n\nIconography\nThe mask is small and has a headdress composed of five cobras. The cobra-hoods form a diadem, referred to as vattuva in Sinhalese. The cobras are painted predominantly in red with a few lines in reddish-yellow. The eyes are small and deep set. The eyebrows are also deep set and painted with petal designs."
      ],
      "dataProvider": [
        "Museum of Ethnography"
      ],
