      "dcDescription": [
        "1916.09.0017 Sri Lanka Ceylon 1916.9.17\n\nName and identification of character\nThe mask appears to depict a member of the vädda-group, possibly a vädda princess, vädi kumari (Sin.). \n\nContext\nThis character appears in the story portion in Kolam performances.\n\nMaterial\nWood, vel-kaduru (Nux vomica).\n\nIconography\nThe diadem is a low headdress, baga otunna (Sin.). \n\nBoth feminine and masculine features are combined in the mask. The elongated earlobes and the earrings suggest a female character. But the piercing eyes are those of a male. \n\nThe dark-green colour of the face is the traditional colour"
      ],
